title: 'POD: stop() does not mention that watches are detached'
updated: 2026-08-13T02:18:21Z
---

Fallout from 17. The =method stop POD in Controller.pm says it stops registered watches and drops pending work, which is still accurate but no longer complete: a stopped watch is now also detached from the client, so a watcher handle a caller kept from watch_resource is left without a parent. Related sharp edge worth a sentence: calling start on such a stale handle drives a loop-less notifier, and the controllers own start() builds a fresh watcher regardless, so keeping the handle across a stop is not useful. Lane: nak-pod-writer.
